Here's the fifteenth disc in a series of mixtapes I made for Laurel's birthday a couple years gone.

https://open.spotify.com/user/steelwagstaff/playlist/7k7ZC2sxxpEqUgkIoatTQu

&nbsp;

Here's the nineteenth in a big collection of mixtapes I made for Laurel's name day a few years ago.

https://open.spotify.com/user/steelwagstaff/playlist/0PQS9TLYNNdmA4LCs9qBEJ

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

<small>Photo by <a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/31846825@N04/15730660483" target="_blank" rel="noopener">State Library and Archives of Florida</a> </small>

Here are 50 songs that I listened to and enjoyed in May 2016. It was a pretty average month for me, musically, but with some fun discoveries. I really liked Cicada Rhythm (a southern folk duo who sound like The Tallest Man on Earth with cello added--beautiful combination), Connie Converse (an almost unknown 1950s singer-songwriter with a fascinating, tragic story), Cotton Jones (indie folk band from Maryland), and The Memories (a couple of stoner bros from Portland whose song "You Need A Big Man" is both ridiculous and feels like the kind of 1 minute long Safety Dance-inspired novelty song everybody needs to start off their summer right).

https://open.spotify.com/user/steelwagstaff/playlist/1XBeUhhwZt0vtm89xO1flO

&nbsp;

Here are 100 songs I listened to and enjoyed in July 2016. It was a very excellent month, sonically. Let these sounds wash over you, friends

https://open.spotify.com/user/steelwagstaff/playlist/61wVH1c8dogoGLisUbDeJ2

&nbsp;

Brace yourself, because it's a lot of music coming here: 145 songs I listened to and enjoyed in August 2016. So much good sound in my ears this month. We joined Spotify family premium, which meant that I listened to a lot more music (no more annoying advertisements! high quality streaming audio! hooray!) in August. The total playlist clocks in just over ten hours long this month, and is totally worth it. Enjoy!

https://open.spotify.com/user/steelwagstaff/playlist/1Sfw1XoERrciGAF6pUFGwI

&nbsp;

Here are 95 songs I listened to and enjoyed in October 2017. Records I had on repeat included John Kennedy's <em>HA!</em>, Balmorhea's <em>Clear Language</em>, Alabama Shakes' <em>Sound &amp; Color</em>, Ane Brun's <em>Leave Me Breathless</em>, Strand of Oaks' <em>HEAL</em>, Langhorne Slim's <em>Life is Confusing</em> EP, and Willie Watson's <em>Folksinger</em> (vol. 1 &amp; 2).

https://open.spotify.com/user/steelwagstaff/playlist/6VzVVBn86Uuoauy20T2fuF

&nbsp;

Here's a playlist of 6+ hours of music I listened to and enjoyed in November 2017. Records I especially enjoyed included Blick Bassy's <em>Ako</em>, Mavis Staples' <em>If All I Was Was Black</em>, Brittany Howard's Thunderbitch record,Mickhael Paskalev's <em>What's Life Without Losers</em>, Landhorne Slim's <em>Lost at Last</em>, Joan Shelley's <em>Ginko</em>, Dom La Nena's <em>Soyo</em>, Max Richter's <em>From Sleep</em>, Jordan Klassen's <em>Monastery</em>, Hiss Golden Messenger's <em>Bad Debt</em>, Little Scream's <em>The Golden Record</em>, and Vic Chestnutt's work on the Mitte Ende August soundtrack,

https://open.spotify.com/user/steelwagstaff/playlist/4RjbB0JiO9itBOExO2TQhW

&nbsp;

Here's a playlist of 40 songs I listened to and enjoyed in December 2017. It was a quieter month for me musically than usual, with end of semester deadlines and vacation, but it was still pleasant and full of some new discoveries that will stick with me for a while. Hope you enjoy!

https://open.spotify.com/user/steelwagstaff/playlist/6XTTT4sFNMZYl81B9vQieu

&nbsp;

Here's a playlist of just under five hours of music I listened to and enjoyed in April 2018 (a lot of it as I was finishing up my dissertation).

https://open.spotify.com/user/steelwagstaff/playlist/7mwWUwyihjhfHBzuEavlNH?si=oPc8j1R7QwirOzaBGxSazA

&nbsp;
